text:
Ben: Quick anomaly report — our staging integration started returning repeated 401s for embedding requests from the Python SDK. The SDK was doing exponential backoff retries and we saw a spike in failed attempts. Anyone else?

Clara: Which kind of 401? Plain auth failed vs insufficient_scope? Can you paste the response body (sanitized)?

Ben: Body was: `{"error":"insufficient_scope","required":"embeddings:write"}`. Interestingly the first request after rotation returned 429 from our gateway, then the SDK retried and got 401s.

Ivy: That sequence matters. If a rotate happens at the edge and a cached route returns 429, the SDK's retry layer should not turn into a credential refresh unless the response indicates auth failure. Are we conflating 4xx reasons in the retry policy?

Mika: Current SDK default: retry on 429 and 5xx with backoff; do not retry on 401/403. But I remember a change that made some internal clients attempt a short-circuit refresh on ANY 4xx when a credentialProvider exists. That might be over-eager.

Ben: We do have a credentialProvider configured in staging so the SDK attempted to call provider() when it saw the 429, because of a bug in classification code `isRetryable(status)` returning true for 4xx ranges in one branch.

Clara: Ah. Bug then. Two things to do: 1) tighten classification so only 429 and 5xx are retryable; 2) decouple "auth refresh" from generic retry. Auth refresh should trigger only on explicit auth failures (401 with bearer challenge or JSON body indicating insufficient_scope/invalid_token) or on 403 with explicit token-related message.

Ivy: Agree. Also, for streaming connections we should have a separate flow: on connect failure with 401/insufficient_scope -> call provider() to get new token and attempt single reconnect. Don't blob that into the generic request retry loop.

Mika: For SDK parity: propose standard behavior across runtimes: - On 401/invalid_token or `error: insufficient_scope` -> call credentialProvider once, if it returns different token then retry the operation once. If still 401 -> surface to caller. - On 403 (permission denied) do NOT refresh, surface immediately. - On 429/5xx -> apply exponential backoff retries (no credential refresh).

Ben: That aligns with our security posture. Also suggests we need two telemetry events: `auth.refresh_attempted` and `auth.refresh_succeeded/failed` so we can later look at rotation pain. Sampleapps can log when they notice refreshes.

Clara: Small sample snippet (JS pseudo) we can add to SDK docs: ```js
async function requestWithAuthWrap(req) {
  let resp = await rawRequest(req);
  if (isAuthError(resp)) {
    const newKey = await credentialProvider();
    if (newKey && newKey !== currentKey) {
      setKey(newKey);
      resp = await rawRequest(req);
    }
  }
  return resp;
}
```

Ivy: Also flagging edge-case: project-scoped vs org-scoped keys. If provider returns a key with narrower scopes (tightened during rotation) we should surface a clear message about insufficient_scope rather than silently retrying. I recommend the SDK attach `X-Redwood-Auth-Attempt:provider` header on retry attempts so we can trace refresh path in logs.

Mika: Good idea. And add a debug-level log entry listing status code and classification decision. Keeps ops from guessing.

Ben: From the sampleapp side: I'll add a small doc in the repo about what the SDK does on auth failures and a troubleshooting section showing how to reproduce rotation issues (rotate key in console, try stream vs simple request). New hires hit this often.

ops-bot: Created ticket DEVX-2988: "SDK retry/auth classification fix + auth-refresh semantics + telemetry + sampleapp cookbook" and added checklist.

Clara: Action items: Mika -> fix classification + implement auth-refresh-one-retry across SDKs; Ivy -> add X-Redwood-Auth-Attempt header and telemetry events; Ben -> sampleapp doc and repro snippets; DevEx -> add a console rotation hint that reminds owners to keep scopes stable or update clients. Will track under DEVX-2988.

Mika: I'll target a small patch to Python/Node this sprint, with a spec PR for Go/Java. Expect initial PR by mid-week.

Ivy: One more thing: add a short entry in the API docs that lists which errors are safe to retry vs when to refresh creds. This will reduce noisy oncall DMs.

Ben: Thanks all — saved us a noisy pager. I'll upload sanitized logs to the ticket. :+1:
